    "content": "Lauren Betts' dad is Andy Betts, a 7-foot-1 former professional basketball player and English national team center. Drafted 50th overall in the 1998 NBA Draft by the Charlotte Hornets, he played for 14 years across Europe—including stops in Spain, Italy, and Greece—before retiring in 2011 to focus on family. Key Facts About Andy Betts: College Career: Played for Long Beach State, where he met his ex-wife, Michelle, a standout volleyball player. European Career: Competed for top-tier clubs including Real Madrid, AEK Athens, and Joventut Badalona, winning a EuroCup and national league titles. International: Represented England and Great Britain for 13 years with 62 caps, playing in the 2009 Eurobasket. Family: Moved to Colorado with his family after his playing career; he and Michelle raised Lauren and her siblings in Europe before settling in the U.S.. Family Height: His son, Dylan, and daughter, UCLA teammate Sienna, also possess basketball talent, with the children inheriting their height from him.",
